        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="files" class="docs-section">
      <h2 class="docs-h2">Where files live</h2>
      <p class="docs-p">Downpick keeps everything in one folder in your home directory. Nothing goes to a server.</p>
      <div class="deftable">
        <div class="filerow">
          <div class="filerow-path">~/.downpick/vault.enc</div>
          <div class="filerow-body">The encrypted vault: connections, database passwords, AI keys. A previous copy is kept as <span class="mono">vault.enc.bak</span>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="filerow">
          <div class="filerow-path">~/.downpick/settings.json</div>
          <div class="filerow-body">Vault path, query timeout, and auto-lock. Holds no secrets, so it's plain text.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="filerow">
          <div class="filerow-path">~/.downpick/chats.db</div>
          <div class="filerow-body">Your saved <a href="#ai-providers">Ask AI conversations</a> — questions and answers, in plain text and outside the vault. Clear them from the history in the AI panel.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="docs-fine">Your open tabs are a separate, in-app preference and are stored in plain text — turn off tab restoration if your query text is sensitive.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <div class="help">
        <div>
          <h2 class="help-title">Still stuck?</h2>
          <p class="help-body">Open an issue on GitHub. Include what you did, what you expected, and the error text verbatim.</p>
        </div>
